.00&amp;quot;),&amp;quot; to &amp;quot;,TEXT(R[0]C[-1],&amp;quot;$#,##0.00&amp;quot;), &amp;quot; per &amp;quot;,(if(R[0]C[-4]=&amp;quot;Exempt&amp;quot;,&amp;quot;year.&amp;quot;,&amp;quot;hour.&amp;quot;)))&quot;&gt;#LI-BF1&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Actual compensation is based on multiple factors that are unique to each candidate, including and not limited to skill set, level of relevant experience, and specific work location.&amp;nbsp; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Salary ranges for positions based in other locations may differ based on the cost of labor in that location.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;For more information about Justworks’ Total Reward Philosophy, including all of the perks and benefits we are proud to offer our team members, please visit &lt;/span&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.justworks.com/careers#total-reward-philosophy&quot;&gt;Total Rewards @ Justworks&lt;/a&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h1&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Diversity At Justworks&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h1&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Justworks is committed to maintaining a workplace where diversity of identity, culture, and life experience is the norm and is celebrated authentically and respected consistently. Diversity in our work, our people, and our product drives creativity and innovation, entrepreneurial leadership and integrity, competitiveness, and collaboration throughout our business and in the market. We depend on our differences to make our team stronger, our workplace more dynamic, and our product accessible to all of our customers.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We’re proud to be an equal opportunity employer open to all qualified applicants regardless of race, color, ancestry, religion, sex, national origin, sexual orientation, age, citizenship, marital or familial status, disability, pregnancy, gender identity or expression, veteran status, genetic information, or any other legally protected status. Justworks is fully dedicated to providing necessary support to candidates with disabilities who may require reasonable accommodations. We also provide reasonable accommodations to employees based on their sincerely held religious beliefs, as well as for other covered reasons consistent with applicable federal, state, and local laws. If you&#39;re in need of a reasonable accommodation, please reach out to us at &lt;a href=&quot;mailto:accommodations@justworks.com&quot;&gt;accommodations@justworks.com&lt;/a&gt;. Your comfort and success matter to us, and we&#39;re here to ensure an inclusive experience.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.justworks.com/press/company-news/justworks-impact-report-2024&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Our DEIB Report&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;h1&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who We Are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h1&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;At Justworks, you’ll enjoy a welcoming and casual environment, great benefits, wellness program offerings, company retreats, and the ability to interact with and learn from leaders in the startup community. We work hard and care about our most prized asset - our people.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;We’re helping businesses get off the ground by enabling them to focus on running their business. We solve HR issues. We’re data-driven and never stop iterating. If you’d like to work in a supportive, entrepreneurial environment, are interested in building something meaningful and having fun while doing it, we’d love to hear from you.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;We&#39;re united by shared goals and shared motivations at Justworks. These are best summed up in our company values, which are reflected in our product and in our team.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.justworks.com/careers#values&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Our Values&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;If this sounds like you, you’ll fit right in.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 18pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who You Are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You’re a seasoned compliance leader who knows that strong regulatory functions depend on clear ownership, capable teams, disciplined execution, and sound judgment. You bring meaningful experience leading regulatory compliance operations in a highly regulated environment. You can translate complex requirements into practical processes, challenge and support subject matter experts, and build the management systems needed to execute regulatory obligations consistently. You are equally comfortable developing teams, engaging with regulators and external partners, partnering with Legal and business leaders, and communicating risks and priorities to senior leadership. You enjoy strengthening functions that are evolving, creating clarity where processes or ownership are fragmented, and building a culture of accountability, collaboration, and continuous improvement.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 18pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Your Success Profile&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 14pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What You Will Work On&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Lead Regulatory Compliance and Licensing&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Provide people and operational leadership across Regulatory Compliance and Licensing Operations within Product Compliance.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Set clear priorities, ownership, operating rhythms, and performance expectations across the functions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop team members and build the capabilities, judgment, and accountability needed for consistent regulatory execution.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with Product Compliance leadership on organizational design, resourcing, and the continued evolution of these functions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Strengthen the Operating Foundation&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Establish clear ownership, documented processes, effective controls, escalation paths, and backup coverage for critical regulatory obligations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Reduce single points of failure through cross-training, business continuity planning, and sustainable knowledge management.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Improve visibility into upcoming obligations, execution status, risks, and issues requiring leadership attention.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Standardize and simplify workflows where doing so improves reliability, efficiency, and compliance outcomes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop meaningful operational measures that help assess execution, capacity, quality, and risk.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Drive Regulatory Execution and Readiness&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ensure timely, accurate, and compliant execution of key obligations, including PEO and other applicable licensing, CPEO certification, ESAC accreditation, regulatory reporting, government filings, business registrations, regulatory examinations, and agency correspondence.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ensure regulatory obligations are appropriately documented, calendared, assigned, reviewed, and escalated.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Oversee interactions with regulators, government agencies, auditors, and external partners as appropriate, and ensure follow-up actions are completed.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Identify emerging regulatory and operational risks early and ensure appropriate mitigation and escalation.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Lead Regulatory Change&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead the function in monitoring and interpreting relevant regulatory developments and assessing their impact on Justworks’ products and operations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ensure changes are communicated to the appropriate stakeholders and translated into clear operational, product, or control requirements.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with Payroll Compliance, Legal, Product, Engineering, Operations, and other stakeholders to support implementation of new or changing requirements.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Establish clear processes for tracking regulatory change from identification through assessment, ownership, implementation, and closure.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Strengthen Controls and Remediation&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with Product Compliance leadership, Internal Audit, Legal, Finance, Product, Security, and other stakeholders to strengthen controls and address identified risks within the functions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support audit and examination readiness through clear documentation, evidence, ownership, and timely follow-up.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ensure remediation actions owned by the functions are appropriately prioritized, assigned, tracked, and sustained.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Promote proactive risk identification and escalation rather than reliance on reactive issue management.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Partner Across the Business&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build trusted partnerships across Legal, Product, Engineering, Payroll Compliance, Finance, Security, Internal Audit, Customer Success, Government Affairs, and Operations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Serve as a senior advisor on regulatory requirements, operational impacts, risks, and implementation considerations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work with cross-functional partners to ensure regulatory requirements are understood and translated into practical, sustainable business processes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Build and Develop the Team&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build an engaged, high-performing team with clear expectations, strong accountability, and a culture of collaboration.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Coach and develop team members, strengthen bench depth, and create opportunities for growth.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Assess capabilities and capacity, address performance or skill gaps, and inform hiring and resourcing decisions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Create sustainable coverage across critical responsibilities through thoughtful role design, cross-training, and succession planning.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;How You Will Do Your Work&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;br&gt;As Senior Manager, Regulatory Compliance and Licensing, how results are achieved is paramount for your success and ultimately results in our success as an organization. In this role, your foundational knowledge, skills, abilities, and personal attributes are anchored in the following:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Strategic Leadership - &lt;/strong&gt;Set direction for the functions you lead and translate Product Compliance priorities into clear operational plans.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;People Leadership - &lt;/strong&gt;Build, coach, and develop teams while establishing clear expectations and accountability.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Regulatory Judgment - &lt;/strong&gt;Apply strong regulatory and compliance judgment, know when deeper subject matter expertise is required, and ensure risks are appropriately evaluated and escalated.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Operational Excellence - &lt;/strong&gt;Build reliable, scalable processes, controls, documentation, and operating rhythms that reduce operational risk.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Systems Thinking - &lt;/strong&gt;Understand how regulatory requirements, licensing, product development, legal interpretation, controls, and operations intersect.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Risk Management - &lt;/strong&gt;Identify regulatory, operational, and business continuity risks early and drive practical mitigation.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Cross-Functional Influence - &lt;/strong&gt;Build trusted partnerships and drive outcomes across teams without relying solely on direct authority.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Executive Communication - &lt;/strong&gt;Provide clear, concise updates on regulatory priorities, organizational health, risks, and decisions requiring leadership attention.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;br&gt;In addition, all Justworkers focus on aligning their behaviors to our core values known as COGIS. It stands for:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Camaraderie - &lt;/strong&gt;Day to day you can be seen working together toward a higher purpose. You like to have fun. You’re an active listener, treat people respectfully, and have a strong desire to know and help others.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Openness - &lt;/strong&gt;Your default is to be open. You&#39;re willing to share information, understand other perspectives, and consider new possibilities. You’re curious, ask open questions, and are receptive to thoughts and feedback from others.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Grit - &lt;/strong&gt;You demonstrate grit by having the courage to commit and persevere. You’re committed, earnest, and dive in to get the job done well with a positive attitude.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Integrity - &lt;/strong&gt;Simply put, do what you say and say what you&#39;ll do. You’re honest and forthright, have a strong moral compass, and strive to match your words with your actions while leading by example.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Simplicity - &lt;/strong&gt;Be like Einstein: “Everything should be made as simple as possible, but no simpler.”&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 18pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Required&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;10+ years of progressive experience in regulatory compliance, licensing, tax compliance or research, compliance operations, or a related field.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;5+ years of people leadership experience, including leading teams responsible for complex regulatory or compliance obligations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience leading regulatory compliance programs in a highly regulated environment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong regulatory judgment and demonstrated ability to translate complex requirements into operational processes, controls, and clear ownership.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated experience strengthening or scaling compliance operations, including process documentation, business continuity, controls, and performance management.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience working with government agencies, regulators, auditors, Legal, and cross-functional business partners.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated ability to identify and manage regulatory, operational, and business continuity risks.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong people leadership, coaching, and performance management skills.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Exceptional written and verbal communication skills, including the ability to communicate risks and priorities to senior leaders.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven ability to influence and drive outcomes across functions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Preferred&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience in PEO, payroll, HR technology, fintech, SaaS, or another regulated technology-enabled environment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with CPEO certification, ESAC accreditation, state PEO licensing, or similar regulatory programs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience leading regulatory change management, or a comparable regulatory interpretation function.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience strengthening compliance functions through organizational, process, or control improvements.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with internal audit, SOX, SOC, or other control and assurance frameworks.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience using technology, automation, or AI to improve compliance operations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span data-sheets-root=&quot;1&quot;&gt;The base wage range for this position based in our New York City Office is targeted at $147,000.00 - $190,000.00 per year.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: rgb(255, 255, 255);&quot; data-sheets-root=&quot;1&quot;&gt;#LI-Hybrid #LI-MM3&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Actual compensation is based on multiple factors that are unique to each candidate, including and not limited to skill set, level of relevant experience, and specific work location.&amp;nbsp; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Salary ranges for positions based in other locations may differ based on the cost of labor in that location.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;For more information about Justworks’ Total Reward Philosophy, including all of the perks and benefits we are proud to offer our team members, please visit &lt;/span&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.justworks.com/careers#total-reward-philosophy&quot;&gt;Total Rewards @ Justworks&lt;/a&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h1&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Diversity At Justworks&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h1&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Justworks is committed to maintaining a workplace where diversity of identity, culture, and life experience is the norm and is celebrated authentically and respected consistently. Diversity in our work, our people, and our product drives creativity and innovation, entrepreneurial leadership and integrity, competitiveness, and collaboration throughout our business and in the market. We depend on our differences to make our team stronger, our workplace more dynamic, and our product accessible to all of our customers.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We’re proud to be an equal opportunity employer open to all qualified applicants regardless of race, color, ancestry, religion, sex, national origin, sexual orientation, age, citizenship, marital or familial status, disability, pregnancy, gender identity or expression, veteran status, genetic information, or any other legally protected status. Justworks is fully dedicated to providing necessary support to candidates with disabilities who may require reasonable accommodations. We also provide reasonable accommodations to employees based on their sincerely held religious beliefs, as well as for other covered reasons consistent with applicable federal, state, and local laws. If you&#39;re in need of a reasonable accommodation, please reach out to us at &lt;a href=&quot;mailto:accommodations@justworks.com&quot;&gt;accommodations@justworks.com&lt;/a&gt;. Your comfort and success matter to us, and we&#39;re here to ensure an inclusive experience.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.justworks.com/press/company-news/justworks-impact-report-2024&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Our DEIB Report&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;h1&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who We Are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h1&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;At Justworks, you’ll enjoy a welcoming and casual environment, great benefits, wellness program offerings, company retreats, and the ability to interact with and learn from leaders in the startup community. We work hard and care about our most prized asset - our people.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;We’re helping businesses get off the ground by enabling them to focus on running their business. We solve HR issues. We’re data-driven and never stop iterating. If you’d like to work in a supportive, entrepreneurial environment, are interested in building something meaningful and having fun while doing it, we’d love to hear from you.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;We&#39;re united by shared goals and shared motivations at Justworks. These are best summed up in our company values, which are reflected in our product and in our team.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.justworks.com/careers#values&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Our Values&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;If this sounds like you, you’ll fit right in.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 18pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who You Are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You’re a seasoned compliance leader who knows that strong regulatory functions depend on clear ownership, capable teams, disciplined execution, and sound judgment. You bring meaningful experience leading regulatory compliance operations in a highly regulated environment. You can translate complex requirements into practical processes, challenge and support subject matter experts, and build the management systems needed to execute regulatory obligations consistently. You are equally comfortable developing teams, engaging with regulators and external partners, partnering with Legal and business leaders, and communicating risks and priorities to senior leadership. You enjoy strengthening functions that are evolving, creating clarity where processes or ownership are fragmented, and building a culture of accountability, collaboration, and continuous improvement.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 18pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Your Success Profile&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 14pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What You Will Work On&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Lead Regulatory Compliance and Licensing&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Provide people and operational leadership across Regulatory Compliance and Licensing Operations within Product Compliance.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Set clear priorities, ownership, operating rhythms, and performance expectations across the functions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop team members and build the capabilities, judgment, and accountability needed for consistent regulatory execution.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with Product Compliance leadership on organizational design, resourcing, and the continued evolution of these functions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Strengthen the Operating Foundation&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Establish clear ownership, documented processes, effective controls, escalation paths, and backup coverage for critical regulatory obligations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Reduce single points of failure through cross-training, business continuity planning, and sustainable knowledge management.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Improve visibility into upcoming obligations, execution status, risks, and issues requiring leadership attention.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Standardize and simplify workflows where doing so improves reliability, efficiency, and compliance outcomes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop meaningful operational measures that help assess execution, capacity, quality, and risk.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Drive Regulatory Execution and Readiness&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ensure timely, accurate, and compliant execution of key obligations, including PEO and other applicable licensing, CPEO certification, ESAC accreditation, regulatory reporting, government filings, business registrations, regulatory examinations, and agency correspondence.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ensure regulatory obligations are appropriately documented, calendared, assigned, reviewed, and escalated.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Oversee interactions with regulators, government agencies, auditors, and external partners as appropriate, and ensure follow-up actions are completed.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Identify emerging regulatory and operational risks early and ensure appropriate mitigation and escalation.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Lead Regulatory Change&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead the function in monitoring and interpreting relevant regulatory developments and assessing their impact on Justworks’ products and operations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ensure changes are communicated to the appropriate stakeholders and translated into clear operational, product, or control requirements.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with Payroll Compliance, Legal, Product, Engineering, Operations, and other stakeholders to support implementation of new or changing requirements.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Establish clear processes for tracking regulatory change from identification through assessment, ownership, implementation, and closure.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Strengthen Controls and Remediation&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with Product Compliance leadership, Internal Audit, Legal, Finance, Product, Security, and other stakeholders to strengthen controls and address identified risks within the functions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support audit and examination readiness through clear documentation, evidence, ownership, and timely follow-up.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ensure remediation actions owned by the functions are appropriately prioritized, assigned, tracked, and sustained.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Promote proactive risk identification and escalation rather than reliance on reactive issue management.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Partner Across the Business&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build trusted partnerships across Legal, Product, Engineering, Payroll Compliance, Finance, Security, Internal Audit, Customer Success, Government Affairs, and Operations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Serve as a senior advisor on regulatory requirements, operational impacts, risks, and implementation considerations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work with cross-functional partners to ensure regulatory requirements are understood and translated into practical, sustainable business processes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Build and Develop the Team&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build an engaged, high-performing team with clear expectations, strong accountability, and a culture of collaboration.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Coach and develop team members, strengthen bench depth, and create opportunities for growth.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Assess capabilities and capacity, address performance or skill gaps, and inform hiring and resourcing decisions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Create sustainable coverage across critical responsibilities through thoughtful role design, cross-training, and succession planning.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;How You Will Do Your Work&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;br&gt;As Senior Manager, Regulatory Compliance and Licensing, how results are achieved is paramount for your success and ultimately results in our success as an organization. In this role, your foundational knowledge, skills, abilities, and personal attributes are anchored in the following:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Strategic Leadership - &lt;/strong&gt;Set direction for the functions you lead and translate Product Compliance priorities into clear operational plans.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;People Leadership - &lt;/strong&gt;Build, coach, and develop teams while establishing clear expectations and accountability.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Regulatory Judgment - &lt;/strong&gt;Apply strong regulatory and compliance judgment, know when deeper subject matter expertise is required, and ensure risks are appropriately evaluated and escalated.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Operational Excellence - &lt;/strong&gt;Build reliable, scalable processes, controls, documentation, and operating rhythms that reduce operational risk.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Systems Thinking - &lt;/strong&gt;Understand how regulatory requirements, licensing, product development, legal interpretation, controls, and operations intersect.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Risk Management - &lt;/strong&gt;Identify regulatory, operational, and business continuity risks early and drive practical mitigation.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Cross-Functional Influence - &lt;/strong&gt;Build trusted partnerships and drive outcomes across teams without relying solely on direct authority.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Executive Communication - &lt;/strong&gt;Provide clear, concise updates on regulatory priorities, organizational health, risks, and decisions requiring leadership attention.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;br&gt;In addition, all Justworkers focus on aligning their behaviors to our core values known as COGIS. It stands for:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Camaraderie - &lt;/strong&gt;Day to day you can be seen working together toward a higher purpose. You like to have fun. You’re an active listener, treat people respectfully, and have a strong desire to know and help others.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Openness - &lt;/strong&gt;Your default is to be open. You&#39;re willing to share information, understand other perspectives, and consider new possibilities. You’re curious, ask open questions, and are receptive to thoughts and feedback from others.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Grit - &lt;/strong&gt;You demonstrate grit by having the courage to commit and persevere. You’re committed, earnest, and dive in to get the job done well with a positive attitude.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Integrity - &lt;/strong&gt;Simply put, do what you say and say what you&#39;ll do. You’re honest and forthright, have a strong moral compass, and strive to match your words with your actions while leading by example.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Simplicity - &lt;/strong&gt;Be like Einstein: “Everything should be made as simple as possible, but no simpler.”&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 18pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Required&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;10+ years of progressive experience in regulatory compliance, licensing, tax compliance or research, compliance operations, or a related field.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;5+ years of people leadership experience, including leading teams responsible for complex regulatory or compliance obligations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience leading regulatory compliance programs in a highly regulated environment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong regulatory judgment and demonstrated ability to translate complex requirements into operational processes, controls, and clear ownership.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated experience strengthening or scaling compliance operations, including process documentation, business continuity, controls, and performance management.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience working with government agencies, regulators, auditors, Legal, and cross-functional business partners.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated ability to identify and manage regulatory, operational, and business continuity risks.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong people leadership, coaching, and performance management skills.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Exceptional written and verbal communication skills, including the ability to communicate risks and priorities to senior leaders.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven ability to influence and drive outcomes across functions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Preferred&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience in PEO, payroll, HR technology, fintech, SaaS, or another regulated technology-enabled environment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with CPEO certification, ESAC accreditation, state PEO licensing, or similar regulatory programs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience leading regulatory change management, or a comparable regulatory interpretation function.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience strengthening compliance functions through organizational, process, or control improvements.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with internal audit, SOX, SOC, or other control and assurance frameworks.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience using technology, automation, or AI to improve compliance operations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span data-sheets-root=&quot;1&quot;&gt;The base wage range for this position based in our Tampa Office is targeted at $137,000.00 to $177,000.00 per year.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: rgb(255, 255, 255);&quot; data-sheets-root=&quot;1&quot;&gt;#LI-Hybrid #LI-MM3&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Actual compensation is based on multiple factors that are unique to each candidate, including and not limited to skill set, level of relevant experience, and specific work location.&amp;nbsp; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Salary ranges for positions based in other locations may differ based on the cost of labor in that location.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;For more information about Justworks’ Total Reward Philosophy, including all of the perks and benefits we are proud to offer our team members, please visit &lt;/span&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.justworks.com/careers#total-reward-philosophy&quot;&gt;Total Rewards @ Justworks&lt;/a&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h1&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Diversity At Justworks&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h1&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Justworks is committed to maintaining a workplace where diversity of identity, culture, and life experience is the norm and is celebrated authentically and respected consistently. Diversity in our work, our people, and our product drives creativity and innovation, entrepreneurial leadership and integrity, competitiveness, and collaboration throughout our business and in the market. We depend on our differences to make our team stronger, our workplace more dynamic, and our product accessible to all of our customers.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We’re proud to be an equal opportunity employer open to all qualified applicants regardless of race, color, ancestry, religion, sex, national origin, sexual orientation, age, citizenship, marital or familial status, disability, pregnancy, gender identity or expression, veteran status, genetic information, or any other legally protected status. Justworks is fully dedicated to providing necessary support to candidates with disabilities who may require reasonable accommodations. We also provide reasonable accommodations to employees based on their sincerely held religious beliefs, as well as for other covered reasons consistent with applicable federal, state, and local laws. If you&#39;re in need of a reasonable accommodation, please reach out to us at &lt;a href=&quot;mailto:accommodations@justworks.com&quot;&gt;accommodations@justworks.com&lt;/a&gt;. Your comfort and success matter to us, and we&#39;re here to ensure an inclusive experience.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.justworks.com/press/company-news/justworks-impact-report-2024&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Our DEIB Report&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;h1&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who We Are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h1&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;At Justworks, you’ll enjoy a welcoming and casual environment, great benefits, wellness program offerings, company retreats, and the ability to interact with and learn from leaders in the startup community. We work hard and care about our most prized asset - our people.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;We’re helping businesses get off the ground by enabling them to focus on running their business. We solve HR issues. We’re data-driven and never stop iterating. If you’d like to work in a supportive, entrepreneurial environment, are interested in building something meaningful and having fun while doing it, we’d love to hear from you.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;We&#39;re united by shared goals and shared motivations at Justworks. These are best summed up in our company values, which are reflected in our product and in our team.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.justworks.com/careers#values&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Our Values&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;If this sounds like you, you’ll fit right in.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;h1&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the team&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h1&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Justworks Technology Strategy &amp;amp; Operations team helps our Product, Engineering, Design, and Data organizations operate as a connected, high-performing Technology Division. We work across teams and organizational boundaries to connect business strategy with Technology priorities, strengthen how leaders plan and make decisions, and build the systems that enable effective execution as Justworks scales.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Our team operates at the intersection of strategy, technology, and organizational operations. We partner closely with Technology leadership to improve organizational performance, align resources with priorities, and create the clarity and accountability needed to deliver meaningful business outcomes.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h1&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the role&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h1&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As the Senior Manager, Technology Strategy &amp;amp; Planning, you&#39;ll play a critical role in shaping how Justworks&#39; Technology Division plans, operates, and delivers against its strategic priorities. Reporting to the Head of Technology Strategy &amp;amp; Operations, you&#39;ll lead the planning processes, operating mechanisms, and cross-functional initiatives that connect our Product, Engineering, Design, and Data organizations.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You&#39;ll partner closely with senior Technology leaders to translate strategic objectives into organizational plans, evaluate priorities and resource tradeoffs, and improve visibility into performance and execution. You&#39;ll develop a deep understanding of our Product and Engineering organizations, including their roadmaps, technical investments, operating models, and organizational constraints, to help leaders make informed decisions about where and how we invest.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is a hands-on leadership role that requires both strategic judgment and operational depth. You&#39;ll independently identify organizational challenges, develop recommendations, and drive meaningful improvements to how Technology operates. You&#39;ll be responsible for building and continuously evolving the systems that enable effective planning, decision-making, and accountability across the division.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Success in this role means going beyond managing processes or reporting on progress. You&#39;ll be expected to challenge assumptions, connect information across teams, anticipate organizational needs, and create durable solutions that help Technology operate more effectively as the business grows.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h1&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h1&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Lead Technology strategic planning:&lt;/strong&gt; Own and continuously improve annual and quarterly planning processes, translating divisional priorities into clear objectives, operating plans, milestones, and measures of success across Product, Engineering, Design, and Data.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Drive organizational and resource planning:&lt;/strong&gt; Partner with Technology leaders, Finance, and People to connect strategic priorities with headcount, organizational capacity, and resource allocation. Develop the analysis and recommendations needed to inform planning and investment tradeoffs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Own Technology&#39;s operating cadence:&lt;/strong&gt; Design, lead, and evolve the division&#39;s leadership forums, business reviews, planning cycles, and decision-making mechanisms to ensure effective alignment, accountability, and follow-through.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Strengthen organizational performance management:&lt;/strong&gt; Establish and improve the metrics, reporting, and analytical frameworks that provide visibility into Technology&#39;s performance, strategic commitments, organizational health, and execution risks. Translate insights into actionable recommendations for leadership.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Partner deeply with Product and Engineering leadership:&lt;/strong&gt; Understand Product strategy, technical roadmaps, Engineering investments, and organizational dependencies to identify opportunities for improved prioritization, sequencing, resource alignment, and cross-functional execution.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Lead strategic operational initiatives:&lt;/strong&gt; Independently identify, scope, and drive cross-functional initiatives that improve Technology&#39;s operating model, organizational capabilities, and ways of working. Lead work from problem definition through implementation and measurable outcomes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Enable executive decision-making:&lt;/strong&gt; Synthesize complex business, technical, and organizational information into clear executive narratives, recommendations, and decision materials. Anticipate the questions and tradeoffs leadership needs to address and ensure decisions translate into action.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Connect Technology with the broader business:&lt;/strong&gt; Partner with Corporate Strategy, Finance, People, Operations, Revenue, and other functions to align Technology planning, investments, and operating priorities with company-wide objectives.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Drive continuous operational improvement:&lt;/strong&gt; Identify systemic inefficiencies, unclear ownership, and organizational friction. Design scalable solutions that simplify how teams work together, improve decision-making, and strengthen execution without introducing unnecessary process.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Lead organizational change:&lt;/strong&gt; Partner with Technology leadership and cross-functional stakeholders to implement changes to operating models, planning practices, organizational processes, and communication mechanisms, ensuring adoption and sustained impact.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Build organizational capabilities:&lt;/strong&gt; Develop repeatable frameworks, tools, and operating practices that improve how Technology functions at scale, creating systems that continue delivering value beyond individual initiatives or leadership involvement.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h1&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/h1&gt;
&lt;h1&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you will need&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h1&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;7+ years of experience in Technology Strategy, Product Strategy &amp;amp; Operations, Business Operations, strategic planning, management consulting, or related roles within a technology-driven organization.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated experience working within or closely alongside Product and Engineering organizations, with a strong understanding of how Product strategy, technical roadmaps, Engineering investments, and organizational capacity connect to business outcomes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong technical fluency, including an understanding of software development lifecycles, platform investments, technical dependencies, Engineering constraints, and emerging technologies. Ability to engage credibly with Product and Engineering leaders and translate technical considerations into strategic and operational implications.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience owning and improving strategic planning processes, organizational operating models, business reviews, performance management systems, and cross-functional decision-making mechanisms.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong business and financial acumen, including experience evaluating resource allocation, organizational capacity, investment tradeoffs, and operational performance.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated ability to independently structure ambiguous business and organizational problems, develop informed recommendations, and lead complex initiatives through implementation.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience influencing senior and executive stakeholders, navigating competing priorities, challenging assumptions constructively, and driving decisions across organizational boundaries.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong analytical capabilities, with experience developing metrics, evaluating organizational performance, and using quantitative and qualitative data to inform strategic decisions. Advanced spreadsheet skills are expected; experience with SQL or business intelligence tools is a plus.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Exceptional written and verbal communication skills, including the ability to synthesize complex technical, business, and organizational information into compelling executive narratives and actionable recommendations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong systems thinking and organizational judgment, with the ability to identify dependencies, anticipate second-order impacts, and design solutions that improve organizational performance at scale.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience driving organizational change, establishing new operating practices, and building alignment across stakeholders with different priorities and incentives.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated leadership capabilities, including the ability to establish accountability, coach others, and lead cross-functional teams through complex organizational challenges.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A high degree of ownership, intellectual curiosity, adaptability, and comfort operating independently in ambiguous and rapidly evolving environments.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience in high-growth technology organizations or complex industries such as FinTech, Healthcare, or HRTech is a plus.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;div&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The base wage range for this position based in our New York City Office is targeted at $188,000.00 - $242,000.00 per year.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Actual compensation is based on multiple factors that are unique to each candidate, including and not limited to skill set, level of relevant experience, and specific work location.&amp;nbsp; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Salary ranges for positions based in other locations may differ based on the cost of labor in that location.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;For more information about Justworks’ Total Reward Philosophy, including all of the perks and benefits we are proud to offer our team members, please visit &lt;/span&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.justworks.com/careers#total-reward-philosophy&quot;&gt;Total Rewards @ Justworks&lt;/a&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h1&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Diversity At Justworks&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h1&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Justworks is committed to maintaining a workplace where diversity of identity, culture, and life experience is the norm and is celebrated authentically and respected consistently. Diversity in our work, our people, and our product drives creativity and innovation, entrepreneurial leadership and integrity, competitiveness, and collaboration throughout our business and in the market. We depend on our differences to make our team stronger, our workplace more dynamic, and our product accessible to all of our customers.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We’re proud to be an equal opportunity employer open to all qualified applicants regardless of race, color, ancestry, religion, sex, national origin, sexual orientation, age, citizenship, marital or familial status, disability, pregnancy, gender identity or expression, veteran status, genetic information, or any other legally protected status. Justworks is fully dedicated to providing necessary support to candidates with disabilities who may require reasonable accommodations. We also provide reasonable accommodations to employees based on their sincerely held religious beliefs, as well as for other covered reasons consistent with applicable federal, state, and local laws. If you&#39;re in need of a reasonable accommodation, please reach out to us at &lt;a href=&quot;mailto:accommodations@justworks.com&quot;&gt;accommodations@justworks.com&lt;/a&gt;. Your comfort and success matter to us, and we&#39;re here to ensure an inclusive experience.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.justworks.com/press/company-news/justworks-impact-report-2024&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Our DEIB Report&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;h1&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who We Are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h1&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;At Justworks, you’ll enjoy a welcoming and casual environment, great benefits, wellness program offerings, company retreats, and the ability to interact with and learn from leaders in the startup community. We work hard and care about our most prized asset - our people.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;We’re helping businesses get off the ground by enabling them to focus on running their business. We solve HR issues. We’re data-driven and never stop iterating. If you’d like to work in a supportive, entrepreneurial environment, are interested in building something meaningful and having fun while doing it, we’d love to hear from you.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;We&#39;re united by shared goals and shared motivations at Justworks. These are best summed up in our company values, which are reflected in our product and in our team.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.justworks.com/careers#values&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Our Values&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;If this sounds like you, you’ll fit right in.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;h1&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who You Are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h1&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As our Senior Partner Marketing Manager, you’ll be the strategic lead bridging marketing with our Alliances and Integrations teams. You’re a strategist—designing partnerships with marketing at the center, ensuring our brand shows up powerfully, and driving coordinated delivery across the organization.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You thrive on building scalable systems and repeatable processes. You&#39;re comfortable working with ambiguity and bringing clarity through data-driven insights and strategic thinking. You see gaps in how work gets done and take initiative to improve processes. You communicate complex partnership dynamics in clear, simple terms, and you&#39;re equally at home discussing channel strategy with executives or optimizing a campaign workflow with marketing ops.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;You’ll own two core areas:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Alliance Partnerships&lt;/strong&gt; – Work alongside our Alliances team to represent marketing in strategic partner deals. You’ll ensure brand and positioning requirements are built into contracts, oversee marketing’s representation on partner channels, and coordinate cross-functional delivery when deals close.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Technology Integrations&lt;/strong&gt; – Drive programs that attract developers and tech partners to build on our platform. Manage co-marketing initiatives, coordinate promotional campaigns with partners, and build the marketing strategy to position Justworks as an attractive partner ecosystem.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Key Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Alliances:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with the Alliances team early in deal cycles to identify marketing requirements and opportunities&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Establish marketing contract terms, brand guidelines, and co-branding standards with strategic partners&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Oversee Justworks’ presence on partner surfaces—websites, app stores, integrations marketplaces, and co-marketing materials&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Coordinate go-to-market execution across marketing when new partnerships launch&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Track partner marketing performance, ROI, and renewal signals to inform strategic decisions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Integrations:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop and execute marketing strategy to attract technology partners and developers to our platform&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Design co-marketing programs and promotional campaigns that drive partner adoption and customer discovery&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Oversee partner marketing assets—integration docs, case studies, webinars, API marketing collateral—to position partners for success&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build relationships with key tech partners to ensure their marketing needs are understood and met&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate with product, partnerships, and sales to align on roadmap priorities and integration marketing lifecycle&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h1&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What We’re Looking For&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h1&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strategic thinking with hands-on execution. You don’t just design strategy—you can roll up your sleeves and ensure it gets implemented. You bridge silos naturally.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partnership marketing expertise. You have 7+ years in B2B/SaaS environments, with proven success in alliance marketing, partner programs, developer ecosystems, or integration strategies.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong stakeholder management. You’re comfortable navigating competing priorities between Alliances, Integrations, Marketing, and Sales teams. You communicate impact in business terms.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Go-to-market experience. You’ve owned or significantly contributed to partner GTM planning, asset creation, campaign execution, and measurement.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Comfort with complexity. You can track and manage multiple partner relationships and integrations simultaneously without losing strategic focus.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Analytical mindset. You measure program performance, know how to define success for different partner types, and aren’t afraid of data.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;In addition, all Justworkers align their behaviors to our core values, known as COGIS:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Camaraderie &lt;/strong&gt;– You work collaboratively toward shared goals. You&#39;re an active listener, treat people respectfully, and build genuine relationships with partners and colleagues.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Openness&lt;/strong&gt; – Your default is to be open. You share information freely, consider multiple perspectives, and welcome feedback from partners and teammates.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Grit &lt;/strong&gt;– You demonstrate commitment and perseverance. You dive in with a positive attitude and see challenges through to resolution.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Integrity &lt;/strong&gt;– You do what you say and say what you&#39;ll do. You&#39;re honest and transparent, especially when managing partner expectations or delivering difficult feedback.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Simplicity &lt;/strong&gt;– You make complex partnership strategies and marketing initiatives simple and easy to understand for partners, colleagues, and stakeholders.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Why Join&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You’ll build partner marketing from the ground up in a scaling organization. You’ll have real autonomy, work closely with executive leadership, and directly influence company growth through strategic partnerships.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;p1&quot;&gt;The base wage range for this position based in our New York City Office is targeted at $166,000 - $214,000 per year.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;p1&quot;&gt;&lt;span data-sheets-root=&quot;1&quot;&gt;#LI-Hybrid #LI-AM2&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
